====================================================================================================
B. explicit escapes with minimal loops (layered DP, s <= 80)
  loops with K = K0(s) found for all 2 <= s <= 80 (HYP-9122 instances), K*(1)=2 (trivial loop)
  972 escapes executed move by move on random integers (legality asserted): endpoint = Psi(m) = 2^K* u exactly, for every k <= 81
  digit consumption: on each shell {v_3(x-h)=k}, x mod 3^(n+k) determines Psi(x) mod 3^n, uniformly onto the units (checked k<=5, n<=4): every Psi step consumes exactly k ternary digits
====================================================================================================
C. optimality inside k moves (inherited Prop 2.1 / Lemma 7.2), brute force over all legal paths
  160 random shells (k=3..6): least endpoint over all legal paths of length <= k equals Psi(m); > m on the 1/2 class, < m on the 1 class
====================================================================================================
D. the frontier-item-1 recursion versus the optimal transfer
  the frontier route (3, loop(k-2), 0) is legal and lands at 2^(K*(k-2)+2) w (checked, k=4..81);
  it equals the optimal landing 2^(K0(k-1)) w iff K0(k-1) = K0(k-2)+2; it is twice as large for 32 of 78 k (fraction 0.410; limit 2 - log2 3 = 0.415), e.g. k = [5, 8, 10, 13, 15, 17, 20, 22]
  optimal recursion on the 1/2 thread:  w' = (2^(K0(k-1)+1) w - 1)/3^k'   (frontier: 2^(K_t+3), K_t=K0(k-2))
====================================================================================================
E. universal landing recursion on random Psi-orbits (big integers)
  3300 consecutive steps: u_(t+1) = (2^(a_t) u_t - h_(t+1)) / 3^(k_(t+1)) with a_t = K*(k_t - 1) + [h_t = 1/2]
====================================================================================================
F. thread table: Psi-itineraries of the known threads and of the 98-point census
  all 98 census points reach 1 or 1/2 exactly, every prefix multiplier > 1; terminals: 1 -> 63, 1/2 -> 35; max itinerary length 3 steps, max digits 26
  max over threads and precisions of ln(link price)/digits = 0.114395 <= c* = 0.114395
  known threads (value, itinerary [class@precision], digits D_h, multiplier P_h, terminal):
         1/2 = 0.5000:   (base point)  D=0 P=1 -> 1/2
       43/32 = 1.3438:          1/2@3  D=3 P=32/27 -> 1
       59/64 = 0.9219:          1/2@3  D=3 P=32/27 -> 1/2
     145/128 = 1.1328:          1/2@4  D=4 P=128/81 -> 1
     209/256 = 0.8164:          1/2@4  D=4 P=128/81 -> 1/2
     371/256 = 1.4492:          1/2@5  D=5 P=256/243 -> 1
     499/512 = 0.9746:          1/2@5  D=5 P=256/243 -> 1/2
  Psi-lift lemma: 6984 random integers m with v_3(m - h) = j > D_h follow h's itinerary exactly and land at tau + 3^(j-D_h) 2^(A_h) W / 2^e  (A_h = log2(P_h 3^D_h))
  link landing y' = 2^(A_h + a_tau(j - D_h)) W / 2^e exactly (a_tau(k) = K*(k-1) + [tau = 1/2]); link multiplier 2^(A_h + a_tau(j-D_h)) / 3^j
  => a repeated landing at a thread h'' = p''/2^e'' with precision j'' has W'' = (2^(A_h + a_tau(j-D_h) + e'' - e) W - p'') / 3^j''

