### 3. Diophantine inputs (LTE, Yu, Senge-Straus/Stewart, digit-exhausted family) and renewal structure
====================================================================================================
K. LTE in 3-adic form and the digits of alpha_w = -log(w')/log 4
  checked v_3(2^n w - 1) = [n=n0 mod 2](1 + v_3((n-n0)/2 - alpha_w)) for all w < 400 (3 !| w), n < 600: 79800 cases
  excess depth max_(1<=M<3^20) v_3(M - alpha_w) - 20 over w < 400: max 4 (w=341), distribution [-1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4]
  (w a power of 4 times 1 or 2: alpha_w is a non-positive integer and v_3 = 1 + v_3(M + a) exactly; otherwise alpha_w is a 3-adic irrational and the depth is the length of a digit coincidence)
    alpha_1   mod 3^20 digits (low first): 00000000000000000000
    alpha_2   mod 3^20 digits (low first): 22222222222222222222
    alpha_4   mod 3^20 digits (low first): 22222222222222222222
    alpha_5   mod 3^20 digits (low first): 02122012201100201021
    alpha_7   mod 3^20 digits (low first): 10210212122110201220
    alpha_11  mod 3^20 digits (low first): 20201102100011110111
    alpha_13  mod 3^20 digits (low first): 21220011202201111021
====================================================================================================
L. Yu's p-adic bound (two logarithms, p = 3), explicit form
  v_3(x1^b1 x2^b2 - 1) < C (log A1)(log A2) max(log T, delta B/B2),  C = (16e)^6 2^1.5 (log 4)^2 3/(log 3)^2 = 9.1448e+10
  applied to 2^n w - p = p (2^(n-r) (2^r w/p) - 1), r in {0,1,2} with 3 !| n-r (so v_3 condition holds):
  v_3(2^n w - p) <= C * 1 * log(4 max(w,p,e)) * (log n + 7 log 3 + 17 + log log 4 max(w,p,e) + 2): O(log n log H)
    n=1e+03 w=1 p=1: Yu bound 1.294e+13   trivial bound n log_3 2 = 6.309e+02   (trivial better)
    n=1e+06 w=7 p=1: Yu bound 2.017e+13   trivial bound n log_3 2 = 6.309e+05   (trivial better)
    n=1e+09 w=1 p=43: Yu bound 3.973e+13   trivial bound n log_3 2 = 6.309e+08   (trivial better)
    n=1e+18 w=1000 p=1: Yu bound 7.117e+13   trivial bound n log_3 2 = 6.309e+17   (Yu better)
====================================================================================================
M. double exhaustion: 2^(a+1) u - 1 = 3^k w' (1/2 thread) and 2^a u - 1 = 3^k w' (1 thread), u odd <= 6000, w' <= 6000, k >= 3, a <= 300
  1/2 thread: 719 solutions; largest n = 2^a u: n=2^9*4117=2107904 = (1+3^6*5783)/2; n=2^10*2423=2481152 = (1+3^7*2269)/2; n=2^11*2305=4720640 = (1+3^8*1439)/2; n=2^12*4433=18157568 = (1+3^11*205)/2
    solutions with n > 10^6: 7; largest a among all: 12
  1 thread: 830 solutions; largest n = 2^a u: n=2^10*4117=4215808 = 1+3^6*5783; n=2^11*2423=4962304 = 1+3^7*2269; n=2^12*2305=9441280 = 1+3^8*1439; n=2^13*4433=36315136 = 1+3^11*205
    solutions with n > 10^6: 16; largest a among all: 13
====================================================================================================
N. digit-exhausted family m = (1 + 3^k w)/2, odd w <= 49, 3 !| w, 3 <= k <= 400 (m up to ~10^192)
  6766 members: all descend under Psi; LTE predicted the second precision exactly in all 398 w=1 cases
  worst excursion 5.0889 at (w,k)=(49, 184);  most Psi-steps 7 at (5, 360);  most L1 digits 403 at (29, 399)
